  "result": "I implemented `slugify` in `src/strings.js` and added 7 tests for it in `test/strings.test.js`. `npm test` passes all 9 tests, including the 2 existing `capitalize` tests.\n\nIt handles đ/Đ first, then strips diacritics, lowercases, and turns each run of non-`a-z0-9` characters into one hyphen. It then trims leading hyphens, cuts to 50 characters, and trims trailing hyphens, so a cut slug never ends in a hyphen. If nothing usable is left, such as for `'!!!'`, it returns an empty string.\n\nThe tests cover basic text, Vietnamese text, đ/Đ, repeated separators and trimming, an empty result, the 50-character limit, and a cut that would otherwise end in a hyphen.",
